            <ArticleTitle>Hereditary angioedema with recurrent abdominal pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>82-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hereditary angioedema is a rare disorder characterized by quantitative or qualitative deficiency of complement C1 esterase inhibitor. We report a family whose members presented with recurrent angioedema and abdominal pain; the diagnosis was confirmed by quantitative assay of C1 inhibitor. The index patient was treated with danazol and was relieved.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
